# P1: invocation-private operand sets

Source-only proposal; no scientific imports, compilation, corpus decoding, correctness execution, timing or implementation performed.

Baseline is PR5995 `4f4159820c37f01d245784d1186bd51fcbc8ebb6`, native C configuration with complete controls. `frozen/scripts/complex_circuit.py` SHA256 is `d623617f7c5cb3189580883a8ab30c0bd3832688ae3f1f0c1f881bbbbff8e0c1`; its `Checks.verify_map` occupies lines 313–333. The frozen caller creates the circuit locally and calls this method once at `complex_network.py:90–93`. This source is distinct from current-main research guidance.

Each of two ordered N-by-N loops constructs both operands anew. At N=2300 the source implies 4N²=21,160,000 operand-set constructions, plus 2N²=10,580,000 intersections. These are operation counts, not timing measurements or a 15% forecast.

## Primary design and preserved checks

Build one exact builtin set per admitted triple, in original positional order, after the untouched node/piece prefix and immediately before the original `nonzero = 0` boundary. Keep these sets private to that invocation and release them on return/error. Use a positional sequence, never a dictionary keyed by triples, so duplicates and ordering are preserved. In each target iteration evaluate every `not (S_set & T_set)` in the first loop and every `len(S_set & T_set) == 2` in the second. Retain both sums, source bit positions, coefficient construction, short-circuit equality assertion, bit counts and exact return dictionary. Do not combine the loops, replace intersection with bit arithmetic/isdisjoint, cache predicate answers, or alter witnesses.

The original independent set operation remains the oracle against constructed support masks. Sharing operand representations does not share any predicate answer. CPython uses a copy when both `&` operands are identical; the diagonal still evaluates the original set intersection expression and produces the same exact set for this callback-free domain. [CPython 3.12.3 set implementation](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/python/cpython/v3.12.3/Objects/setobject.c), `set_intersection`, lines 1099–1140.

## Admission, ownership and fallback

Exact tuple/int checks alone do not establish safety. Lists are mutable, and hashed collections can invoke user hash/equality methods. [Python data model](https://docs.python.org/3.12/reference/datamodel.html#object.__hash__). Sets are mutable distinct-member collections; creating them once changes allocation and callback counts. [Python set documentation](https://docs.python.org/3.12/library/stdtypes.html#set-types-set-frozenset).

Admission requires a **new, scoped whole-tail ownership invariant**, independently established by the parent for this frozen full caller. The original native guard's per-kernel no-mutation promise does not establish it. Capture the actual circuit and Checks identities in the parent-owned construction wrappers, arm one invocation only within the fresh assertion-on CLI, and check an opaque identity record after the prefix. No caller-supplied policy function executes. Deny the lease for unrecognized construction/call boundaries, active mutation hooks, changed source/dispatch, or reentry; use literal fallback. Source-bound exact classes, ordinary attributes, an exact list of exact length-three integer tuples, original builtins and the frozen Fraction environment complete admission. See `OWNERSHIP.md` for issuance, denial and revocation. This is an explicit candidate restriction, not a strengthened claim about baseline Python behavior or generic alias detection.

Run admission after the original prefix, since earlier prefix operations can mutate aliases. Also inspect the local `got` dictionary without custom equality: every key must be an exact pair of an exact integer triple and an exact Fraction with exact integer slot values; every value must be an exact int. Otherwise a custom collision key retained by the prefix could run equality during later lookups and invalidate reuse. Inspect through anchored type/container primitives, never custom iteration or descriptors. Verify the relevant class, function/global/builtin/Fraction resolutions at admission; new checks and any source-binding preparation are paid costs.

Unsupported input or absent ownership lease selects the literal original pairwise tail in the same call, after the already executed prefix. Do not call the complete original method again and repeat prefix callbacks. Binding rejection before executing the prefix may delegate the complete original once. Preserve original exceptions and assertion order; propagate allocation failures without retry. Identical allocation-failure timing is outside the existing resource-bounded execution contract and cannot be promised by an allocation optimization.

## Costs, validation and discriminating test

Remove 4N²−N operand constructions; retain all 2N² intersection allocations/checks. Add source binding, admission scans of N triples and the `got` keys, ownership bookkeeping, N retained sets, positional references, any defensive snapshot/final custody scan, cleanup and finite controls. Runtime and peak-memory costs remain unknown until measured.

Finite fixtures cover intersections 0/1/2/3, duplicates, reordered triples, negative/large ints, empty inputs, exact returns, failed node/piece assertions, custom hash/equality/iterators/subclasses, a custom `got` collision key, prefix mutation, missing/reused lease, between-call mutation and binding drift. Compare error type/args and callback order in fallback; run normal and optimized-interpreter finite controls. The discriminating test is a failing-prefix callback fixture followed by a post-prefix mutation/collision fixture: any eager cache or whole-method fallback must fail these controls. Parent then runs complete baseline/candidate pilots with original certificate, stdout, typed return, witnesses, ranks and complements unchanged. Micro results establish only mechanism; complete fresh native-baseline timing establishes benefit. `CALL-BUDGET.json` separates eliminated metadata construction from retained checks. Intersection-result sharing or loop fusion is a separate unapproved research branch, requiring independence/error-order review.
